able part. Then, we multiply all of the results together.\n\nSo first, we find $\\text{LCM}(4,7):$\n\n- Multiples of $4:$ $\\,4,\\,8,\\,12,\\,16,\\,20,\\,24,\\,28,\\,32,…$\n\n- Multiples of $7:$ $\\,7,\\,14,\\,21,\\,28,\\,35,…$\n\nSo, $\\text{LCM}(4,7)=28.$\n\nTo find the $\\text{LCM}$ of $(z+2)^{2}(w-5)^{2}$ and $(z+2)^{3}(w-5)^{4},$ we find the largest powers for $(z+2)$ and $(w-5)$ that appear in the expressions:\n\n- For $(z+2)^{2}$ and $(z+2)^{3},$ the largest power is $3.$\n\n- For $(w-5)^{2}$ and $(w-5)^{4},$ the largest power is $4.$\n\nNow, we raise $(z+2)$ and $(w-5)$ to the corresponding largest powers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}((z+2)^{2}(w-5)^{2},\\,(z+2)^{3}(w-5)^{4})=(z+2)^{3}\\cdot (w-5)^{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply all of our results together:\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(4(z+2)^{2}(w-5)^{2},\\,7(z+2)^{3}(w-5)^{4})=28(z+2)^{3}(w-5)^{4}.\n$$" 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247614 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247615 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247616 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247617 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247618 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1041 "selection" 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247614 13194139533702 true] [17592186247613 1110 #uuid "bce1c5f5-d726-5c2d-a340-a01e965061ea" 13194139533702 true] [17592186247614 1034 "28(z+2)^{3}(w-5)^{4}" 13194139533702 true] [17592186247614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533702 true] [17592186247614 1111 #uuid "506e6fc8-2c55-562b-af61-41f0cb643dbf" 13194139533702 true] [17592186247615 1034 "42(z+2)^{2}(w-5)^{4}" 13194139533702 true] [17592186247615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533702 true] [17592186247615 1111 #uuid "7389b1df-0bf3-5423-946a-115d606fe0da" 13194139533702 true] [17592186247616 1034 "42(z+2)^{2}(w-5)^{5}" 13194139533702 true] [175921